@uezo Thank you for your reply.  
The issue of multibyte characters being replaced by blanks is described below with sample code.

- The "name" and "description" of the script displayed in the script management page will be displayed correctly, including multibyte characters.
- In the script code displayed by "View source" from the script management page, multibyte characters will be blank.
- In the script that is actually executed, multibyte characters will be blank.

```
// ==UserScript==
// @name ⚠test⚠ multibyte characters display.
// @version 0.1.00
// @description ⚠test⚠ en: This is test script. Bromite is a great FLOSS product 👍/ja :これはテスト用スクリプトです。ブロマイトは素晴らしいFLOSS製品です 👍
// @run-at document-end
// ==/UserScript==
'use strict';
(() => {
  alert('English: [This is test script. Bromite is a great FLOSS product 👍]\nJapanese: [これはテスト用スクリプトです。ブロマイトは素晴らしいFLOSS製品です 👍]\n');
  document.body.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend','<div id="test-message-container" style="position:fixed;top:0;height:50px;width:100vw;background:#e33a;display:grid;place-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:10000;"><p>Thumbs Up Emoji:[👍]</p></div>');
}
)();
```

@Disqu3-mirOir-qt is correct, content scripts do not run in the scope of the current page (see https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/mv3/content_scripts/#isolated_world)
try using the run-at clause as described [here](https://github.com/bromite/bromite/wiki/UserScripts)
unlike other browsers, userscripts in bromite are more similar to chrome extensions, if you search on the internet you will find all the details

